title: Implement reexport consent enforcement
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-15T05:51:53'
updated_at: '2026-06-17T00:14:23'
result: 'Reexport-consent dropped per user directive; replaced with a self-declared
  visibility ceiling on the target package (scope.md §4). Two rungs: public (default,
  reach-in open) / internal (visible only within the target''s own owner-scope subtree).
  Implemented Visibility enum + PackageRecord.visibility + ScopePath::is_prefix_of
  + resolve_path_use (multi-segment hop-by-hop resolution gated by a ScopePath prefix
  check) in pkgid.rs; wired into the typer (resolve_scoped_path_use, UseLocal multi-segment
  lowering); parsed `visibility` manifest key in ProjectConfig and threaded it through
  dag.rs/packages.rs into PackageRecord. Docs updated in lockstep (scope.md, config-blocks.md,
  lamp.md, lamp-prereqs.md). +11 tests (5 pkgid unit, 3 dag end-to-end via real project.jn
  manifests, 3 reused). Build warning-clean; full suite green except 3 pre-existing
  unrelated @column integration failures.'
description: Enforce that 'use baz/bar' is legal only when baz explicitly declares
  reexport of bar; any reach-in without consent is a hard error. Done when reexport
  declarations are parsed/recognized, consented reexports resolve, and reach-in attempts
  produce hard errors verified by tests. Depends on path-scoped use resolution subtask.
